# AI Provider Tycoon — Mechanics Overview

Three levels of zoom on the same system.

## Level 1 — The economic loop

The core round-robin. Cash funds spend, spend builds capabilities, capabilities win market share, market share generates revenue, revenue refills cash. Situations perturb the loop from outside.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Cash[💰 Cash]
    Spend[Spend lines]
    Caps[Capabilities<br/>Brand · Quality · Capacity]
    Market[Demand share]
    Rev[Revenue]

    Cash -->|funds| Spend
    Spend -->|builds| Caps
    Caps -->|drives| Market
    Market -->|served| Rev
    Rev -->|refills| Cash

    Situations((⚡ Situations)):::sit -.-> Caps
    Situations -.-> Market
    Situations -.-> Cash

    classDef sit fill:#ffe6cc,stroke:#d79b00
```

## Level 2 — Player decisions → state

What every action category affects. Spend lines feed burn; capability-building actions move state directly.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Actions["Player actions"]
        direction TB
        Marketing[Marketing spend]
        ResearchSpend[Research spend]
        ReliabilitySpend[Reliability spend]
        BuyServer[Buy / sell servers]
        SetPrice[Set price]
        Publish[Publish model]
        VC[VC raise]
        Ops[Certifications · Security · Privacy]
        Inter[M&A · Messaging · Sabotage]
    end

    subgraph State["Player state"]
        direction TB
        BrandS[Brand]
        QualityS[Model quality]
        CapacityS[Servers · Capacity]
        OpsS[Ops levels]
        CashS[Cash]
        BurnS[Burn rate]
    end

    Marketing --> BrandS
    Marketing --> BurnS
    ResearchSpend --> QualityS
    ResearchSpend --> BurnS
    ReliabilitySpend --> OpsS
    ReliabilitySpend --> BurnS
    BuyServer --> CapacityS
    BuyServer --> CashS
    SetPrice -.->|exposed to market| BrandS
    Publish --> QualityS
    VC --> CashS
    Ops --> OpsS
    Inter -.->|targets others| BrandS
    Inter -.->|targets others| OpsS
    BurnS -->|drains| CashS
```

## Level 3 — Situations & counters

Situations are server-generated shocks, polarised on two axes (scope × sign). Pre-bought capabilities (mostly Operations) reduce, null, or flip them.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph Sit["Situation"]
        direction TB
        Polarity{Polarity}
        Polarity --> GN[Global<br/>Negative]
        Polarity --> CN[Conditional<br/>Negative]
        Polarity --> CP[Conditional<br/>Positive]
        Polarity --> GP[Global<br/>Positive]
    end

    subgraph Prereqs["Pre-bought prerequisites"]
        direction TB
        Reliability
        IncidentResponse[Incident response]
        SecurityP[Security level]
        Certs[Certifications]
        PrivacyP[Privacy level]
        EfficiencyP[Efficiency upgrades]
        PositioningP[Positioning]
    end

    subgraph Effects["Effect on player"]
        direction TB
        Damage[Damage]
        Skip[No effect]
        Benefit[Benefit]
    end

    GN --> Damage
    CN -->|no prereq| Damage
    CN -->|prereq met| Skip
    CP -->|prereq met| Benefit
    CP -->|no prereq| Skip
    GP --> Benefit

    Prereqs -.->|reduce<br/>severity| GN
    Prereqs -.->|gate| CN
    Prereqs -.->|gate| CP
```
